        ,
          "choices": ["trunc", "round"]
        },
        {
          "param": "m",
          "low": 2,
          "high": 8
        ,
          "choices": null
        }
      ],
      "budget_share": 0.35,
      "why": "Pipelined_m registers every m stages, reducing FF count and potentially improving Fmax compared to fully pipelined by breaking the long chain. Still 1 result/cycle. The m parameter allows trading off latency for area/timing. We search m=2..8 to find the best Fmax/LUT tradeoff. This is the most promising family for meeting 400 MSPS with minimal LUTs."
    },
    {
      "family": "unrolled_k",
      "ranges": [
        {
          "param": "data_width",
          "low": 12,
          "high": 18
        ,
          "choices": null
        },
        {
          "param": "n_iter",
          "low": 12,
          "high": 18
